        },
        "prompts": [
          {
            "after": null,
            "at_step": 1,
            "concept": "These eight sequences share a true tree, but the alignment is deliberately short. Build the NJ tree, then step to the end to ask: how sure are we that each grouping is real?",
            "math": "A short internal branch leaves few sites where its grouping differs from the rest — exactly the sites a resample can miss.",
            "reveal": null,
            "reveal_pair": null,
            "type": "note"
          },
          {
            "after": null,
            "at_step": 7,
            "concept": "Before you run, make a prediction: which internal branch of the inferred tree will the data support least? Click that branch — terminal branches don't count — then run the bootstrap.",
            "math": "Each replicate resamples the 300 columns with replacement and rebuilds the tree; a grouping's support is the share of successful replicate trees that contain it.",
            "reveal": "The weakest grouping is the one on the true tree's shortest internal branch. At 300 columns, only a handful of sites carry evidence for it, so many resampled datasets rebuild a different grouping there.",
            "reveal_pair": null,
            "type": "predict_branch"
          },
          {
            "after": "first_run",
            "at_step": 7,
            "concept": "Support is an estimate too. Change the bootstrap Seed and run again: the numbers shift by a few points, because each run draws different resamples. (With 1,000 replicates instead of 100 they settle down — so don't read much into small differences like 52 versus 57.)",
            "math": null,
            "reveal": null,
            "reveal_pair": null,
            "type": "note"
          },
          {
            "after": "continue_or_second_run",
            "at_step": 7,
            "concept": "Now try more data. Raise Length to 3,000 — ten times as many columns — and run again. Watch what happens to that grouping's support.",
            "math": "Signal scales with sites: the same tree under 10× the columns puts ~10× the expected substitutions on every branch, short ones included.",
            "reveal": null,
            "reveal_pair": null,
            "type": "note"
          },
          {
            "after": "longer_run",
            "at_step": 7,
            "concept": "Read the numbers carefully. When a grouping shows 87, it means 87 of 100 resampled datasets rebuilt it, not that it has an 87% chance of being true. Support measures how consistently the data points to a grouping. Low support means this dataset says little about that grouping, not that the grouping is wrong: here the weak grouping was real, and a longer alignment raised its support. Small differences between seeds or runs are noise; don't overinterpret them.",
            "math": null,
            "reveal": null,
            "reveal_pair": null,
            "type": "note"
          }
        ],
